--- BASELINE REPAIRS (pre-existing integration breakage that blocked the solution-wide gate) ---
The HEAD integration merge (aef718030, clean tree) carried two pre-existing defects that broke the
whole-solution build/test gate before any NoVehicleSelected code existed. Both were repaired minimally:
1. MotorStats namespace collision: feature-views/MotorEfficiencyInsights/MotorEfficiencyInsights.Model.cs
   and feature-views/SummaryStats/SummaryStats.Model.cs BOTH declared `public sealed record MotorStats`
   (structurally different shapes) in namespace TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews -> CS0101 + CS8863 -> the C#
   compile failed -> no LocalAssembly -> the XAML compiler cascaded (WMC1509/WMC0001/WMC9999, 83 errors).
   Fix: renamed the SummaryStats record (fewer references) to `SummaryMotorStats` across SummaryStats.Model.cs,
   SummaryStats.ViewModel.cs and SummaryStatsTests.cs (5 + 3 + 9 = 17 precise type references; web-name
   prose `<c>MotorStats</c>` / `motorStats: MotorStats | null` / `computeMotorStats` left intact). The
   MotorEfficiencyInsights record keeps the `MotorStats` name. This was the sole blocker of the whole
   headless suite; the rename is unambiguous and minimal.
2. Two-root test csproj: apps/windows/TeslaSync.App.Tests/TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj had TWO <Project>
   roots concatenated (lines 1-785 and 786-1397) -> invalid XML (MSB4025) -> dotnet test could not load.
   Per the file's own documented INVARIANT, consolidated back to ONE valid <Project> root holding the
   deduplicated, path-sorted union of all 529 previously-linked Compile sources, plus this surface's 2 new
   links (NoVehicleSelected.Model.cs, NoVehicleSelected.ViewModel.cs) = 531 total. No linked source dropped.

